␀Node name␀␀␀Advert location␀Latitude␀␀␀␀Longitude␀␀␀Pick on the map␀Adverts reach every node in range, unencrypted. GPS > Location privacy can shift the position they carry.␀␀␀Share location in advert␀␀␀␀Identity (public key)␀␀␀Hold the key to copy it.␀␀␀␀Share QR␀␀␀␀Add automatically␀␀␀A node you hear an advert from joins Contacts when its type is on here.␀Chat users␀␀Room servers␀␀␀␀Sensors␀0 adds from any distance, 1 only nodes heard directly, and N up to N-1 hops away.␀␀␀Max hops (0..64)␀␀␀␀When Contacts is full␀␀␀A new node replaces the oldest contact. Favourites are never replaced.␀␀Overwrite oldest non-favorite␀␀␀Remove old contacts␀Deletes contacts not heard from in the number of days below. Favourites are never deleted.␀␀Auto-delete old contacts␀␀␀␀Not heard from for this many days, 1 to 999.␀␀␀␀Days␀␀␀␀Notifications␀␀␀A short note on screen when a node is added.␀␀␀␀Notify on new contact␀␀␀Pick one from the quick-reply button beside the message box in any chat. An empty slot is skipped.␀␀Experimental. Slows the processor while the screen is off (Bluetooth and Wi-Fi keep working), lets the GPS rest between position checks and keeps a moving background still.␀␀␀␀Battery & power history␀remote view open␀␀␀␀Battery saver␀␀␀Calibrate as full␀␀␀Tap with a full battery to call its voltage 100%. Hold to go back to the default.␀␀␀A LoRa Update is running for␀␀␀␀LoRa Update␀Firmware file␀␀␀v%u.%u.%u.%u␀␀␀␀v%u.%u.%u␀␀␀%s  %s  %s␀␀îƒŒ␀Refresh␀Build .mota files with Mike Carper's motatool, or download them in MeshCore Open TAK. Use a file made for this repeater's board.␀␀␀␀Temporary radio␀The repeater and this radio meet here for the transfer, away from the normal mesh. Pick a quiet frequency you may use. The repeater must be in direct range.␀␀␀␀Frequency (MHz)␀Bandwidth (kHz)␀Minutes␀Step␀␀␀␀Blocks␀␀Packets sent␀␀␀␀Start update␀␀␀␀Install and reboot␀␀Log␀This radio can't run a temporary radio (its SX1262 signals packets through an I/O expander), so it can't serve updates.␀This radio can't run a temporary radio (needs an SX1262), so it can't serve updates.␀␀␀␀Highly experimental. This forwards the text, sender name and timestamp of every message your node receives to an MQTT broker, where anyone able to read the broker can read them. Direct messages are private messages from other people who never agreed to be shared. Use a broker you control, set an encryption key below, and never a public broker.␀␀␀I accept the privacy risk␀␀␀Enable MQTT bridge␀␀Broker␀␀Broker host / IP␀␀␀␀192.168.1.x␀Port␀␀␀␀1883␀␀␀␀Leave empty if not required␀Username (optional)␀Password (optional)␀Publish␀Publish channel messages␀␀␀␀Other people's private messages to you. Only to a broker you control.␀␀␀Publish direct messages␀Empty = plaintext to a private broker␀␀␀Encryption key (optional)␀␀␀psk␀ïƒ‡␀Nothing above applies until you save.␀␀␀Internal DRAM
